<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="CloudLaunch helps teams build, ship and scale with confidence.">
  <title>CloudLaunch | Build. Ship. Scale.</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="script.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <nav class="nav container" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a class="brand" href="#home"><span class="brand-mark">C</span> CloudLaunch</a>
      <button class="menu-toggle" id="menuToggle" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-expanded="false">☰</button>
      <div class="nav-links" id="navLinks">
        <a href="#features">Features</a>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero" id="home">
      <div class="container hero-content">
        <p class="eyebrow">YOUR IDEAS, IN ORBIT</p>
        <h1>Build boldly.<br><span>Launch confidently.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">A simpler way to turn great ideas into reliable digital experiences. Start small, move fast and keep growing.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#contact">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="#features">Explore features</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-note"><span class="status-dot"></span> Made for teams that keep moving</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-orbit orbit-one"></div>
      <div class="hero-orbit orbit-two"></div>
      <div class="hero-glow"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="features section" id="features">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">WHAT YOU GET</p>
          <h2>Everything you need<br>to move forward.</h2>
          <p>Less friction between the first idea and the finished product.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">↗</div>
            <h3>Move faster</h3>
            <p>Keep your workflow clear and focused, so your team can spend more time creating.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">◇</div>
            <h3>Stay reliable</h3>
            <p>Build with consistency and make improvements with confidence at every step.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">◎</div>
            <h3>Keep growing</h3>
            <p>Start with what you need today and expand as your goals and ambitions grow.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section section" id="about">
      <div class="container about-panel">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A BETTER WAY TO BUILD</p>
          <h2>Big progress starts<br>with one small step.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>CloudLaunch is a sample website built with plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. It is lightweight, responsive and ready for you to customise as your first CI/CD deployment project.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="contact section" id="contact">
      <div class="container contact-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">READY WHEN YOU ARE</p>
        <h2>Let's make something<br><span>worth launching.</span></h2>
        <p>Change this section to add your own email address, business details or call to action.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:hello@example.com">Say hello <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#home"><span class="brand-mark">C</span> CloudLaunch</a>
      <p>© <span id="year"></span> CloudLaunch. Built to go further.</p>
      <a href="#home" class="back-top">Back to top ↑</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
